{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION (carry-over from the previous round, still open): `x@1.2.3.zip` local files are shadowed by registry refs**

The version group of `_registryRef` (`[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*`) still matches the token `1.2.3.zip`, and `isPack()` checks `isRegistryRef` **before** the local-`.zip`-exists branch (line 117). So with a registry configured, a local file literally named `x@1.2.3.zip` is treated as the registry ref `x@1.2.3.zip` and the resolver fetches `$registry/x-1.2.3.zip` instead of using the file on disk — contradicting the doc comment's promise that file paths never match.

Unusual filename, non-urgent; either of the previously proposed fixes closes it:

```dart
// option 1: refuse .zip-suffixed versions
RegExp(r'^([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)@(latest|[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*(?<!\.zip))$');
// option 2: local file wins
if (base.toLowerCase().endsWith('.zip') && File(base).existsSync()) return true;
if (isRegistryRef(base)) return true;
```
"}

{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment3.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION (carry-over from the previous round, still open): no parent-chain cycle guard now that parents can be packs**

`_loadAndResolve` still recurses with no seen-set. Cycles were already possible with filesystem parents (`a.json → b.json → a.json` → stack overflow), but pack refs make them cheaper to hit and more confusing: a pack whose entry config declares `"parent": {"path": "<itself>@1.0.0"}` (or two packs referencing each other) recurses forever, and every hop now also does network fetches + catalog lookups + cache work before the raw `StackOverflowError` surfaces — not a config error.

Since this PR already threads `_packResolver` through the resolver, a cycle set is a small addition:

```dart
// field
final Set<String> _resolving = {};

Map<String, dynamic> _loadAndResolve(String parentPath, String configDir) {
  if (_resolving.contains(parentPath)) {
    throw AgentPackException('Parent cycle detected: $parentPath');
  }
  _resolving.add(parentPath);
  try {
    ... existing body ...
  } finally {
    _resolving.remove(parentPath);
  }
}
```

(plus a test with two configs parenting each other, and optionally two packs).
"}

